{
  "about": "Direct access (docs/direct-access-and-domains.md). Addresses: `canonical` maps input to canonical text (null = not an address); `public`/`notPublic` classify canonical text. Prefixes: `valid` maps input to canonical, `invalid` must not parse, `contains` pins membership. Order: build `order.canonical` byte for byte, its SHA-256 is `order.sha256`; the pinned signature verifies under `keys.adminRootPubHex` and NOT under `keys.irkPubHex`; each `order.refused` entry has the reason code `problem` and must never verify. Address update and hint v2: build `canonical` from `fields`; each case verifies under `keys.stkPubHex` with the box's check against the order (`order` in the case, else the main order; `withOrder: false` = no verified order) and gives `reason` (null = accepted) or `useDirect`. Check time: address cases at `addressUpdate.now`, hint cases at `hintV2.now`, hint expectations `serverDomain` and `certSha256` of the main hint.",
